Algorithm: Car Parking Management Using Linked List
Step 1: Start the program.
Step 2: Define a structure named Node.
Step 3: Store the following information in each node:
Vehicle number
Owner name
Pointer to the next node
Step 4: Initialize head = NULL.
Step 5: Display the parking management menu.
Step 6: Accept the user's choice.
Step 7: If the user selects Add Vehicle:
Create a new node.
Enter the vehicle number.
Enter the owner's name.
Set newNode->next = NULL.
Check whether head == NULL.
If the list is empty, make head = newNode.
Otherwise, start from head.
Traverse the linked list until the last node is reached.
Connect the last node to the new node.
Step 8: If other operations such as display, search, or remove are present in the complete code, perform the selected operation.
Step 9: Continue displaying the menu until the user selects the Exit option.
Step 10: Stop the program.
